1. Work performed

Patched the NVFP4 branch in [linear_op.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp#L455) so `NEMOTRON_FORWARD_LINEAR_DEVICE_FASTPATH=1` now builds the cuBLASLt plan from `BuildRuntimeGemmPlan()` directly, using uploaded `DeviceNvfp4Weight` buffers, instead of probing the descriptor/mmap path first. I also recorded the checkpoint in [PLAN.md](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/proj-2026-04-01-1534/PLAN.md#L347).

2. Root cause confirmed

Yes. [cublaslt_gemm_plan.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/loader/cublaslt_gemm_plan.cpp#L123) rejects NVFP4 plans when packed, block-scale, or tensor-scale pointers are not 16-byte aligned, and the old NVFP4 flow in [linear_op.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp#L455) tried the descriptor plan first, which uses mmap-derived checkpoint offsets. The uploaded runtime weights come from `cudaMalloc`-backed copies in [nvfp4_weight.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_weight.cpp#L34), so that path avoids the host-pointer alignment problem.

3. Compile status

All requested builds passed:
`cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend`
`cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target full_forward_manifest_smoke_test nano_16_token_correctness_test -j4`
`cmake --build build-benchmarks --target nano_fused_decode_bench -j4`

The only failure I hit was a self-inflicted parallel build race from running two `build-phase1-tests` invocations at once; rerunning them sequentially succeeded.

4. Any concerns

I did not add an aligned-buffer workaround to the descriptor-backed NVFP4 path, so non-fastpath descriptor users would still keep the original 16-byte alignment requirement. I also did not rerun the real-model smoke/parity commands in this checkpoint, so the remaining unknown is whether this change fully clears the expert-layer-13 failure on the actual fastpath run.
